{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44116328",
      "title": "Sending Data To A Backend",
      "lectureOrder": 229,
      "videoOrder": 218,
      "sourceHash": "3e69f63199881c3c607ab36706d7286d225b377e43834c758f3aa59ecd4b4c41",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.54,
          "end": 4.05,
          "en": "So we did now learn how to send get requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.05,
          "end": 7.26,
          "en": "and how to fetch data and how to show loading",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.26,
          "end": 10.14,
          "en": "and error state if needed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.14,
          "end": 12.03,
          "en": "Now let's take the next step",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.03,
          "end": 14.4,
          "en": "and let's also send data to the backend,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.4,
          "end": 16.8,
          "en": "not just fetch data from there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.8,
          "end": 18.57,
          "en": "And for that I want to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 18.57,
          "end": 21.84,
          "en": "that if I click one of these places,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 21.84,
          "end": 25.56,
          "en": "request is sent to the backend and this place data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.56,
          "end": 29.49,
          "en": "or some place identifier is sent to the backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.49,
          "end": 32.28,
          "en": "so that there in my backend,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.28,
          "end": 36.15,
          "en": "it's stored in this user-places.json file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.15,
          "end": 39.45,
          "en": "which in the end represents a database table",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.45,
          "end": 43.95,
          "en": "that stores the data of the favorite places a user selected.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.95,
          "end": 48.66,
          "en": "For that, in my backend code, I got this put route here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.66,
          "end": 52.533,
          "en": "This put /user-places route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 53.49,
          "end": 58.49,
          "en": "This route wants a put request, not get, not post, but put.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 59.7,
          "end": 64.17,
          "en": "And then it expects to get the place ID of the place",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 64.17,
          "end": 68.97,
          "en": "that should be stored for the user in the request body.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 68.97,
          "end": 72.84,
          "en": "Because when sending non-get requests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 72.84,
          "end": 76.5,
          "en": "you often have request bodies attached",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 76.5,
          "end": 79.56,
          "en": "to those outgoing requests which carry data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 79.56,
          "end": 81.633,
          "en": "that should be submitted to the backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 82.8,
          "end": 86.49,
          "en": "Therefore here in the available places component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 86.49,
          "end": 90.69,
          "en": "in the template, I have the app-places component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 90.69,
          "end": 95.00999999999999,
          "en": "and that component emits the selectPlace event",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 95.00999999999999,
          "end": 98.223,
          "en": "whenever the user clicks on one of these places.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 99.12,
          "end": 102.15,
          "en": "So in the available places component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 102.15,
          "end": 107.15,
          "en": "we can listen to this selectPlace event on app-places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 109.08,
          "end": 114.06,
          "en": "and then trigger some function on selectPlace, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 114.06,
          "end": 115.593,
          "en": "when that event occurs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 117.09,
          "end": 120.09,
          "en": "It's also worth noting that this event carries",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 120.09,
          "end": 122.793,
          "en": "the place object as data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 124.14,
          "end": 127.98,
          "en": "So we can use the dollar sign event variable here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 127.98,
          "end": 131.58,
          "en": "which is automatically generated and managed by Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 131.58,
          "end": 134.913,
          "en": "to pass that emitted place data onto this method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 136.41,
          "end": 140.91,
          "en": "We have to, however, add that method now as a first step",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 140.91,
          "end": 145.05,
          "en": "to the available places component class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 145.05,
          "end": 148.413,
          "en": "And I'll do that here after ngOnInit, let's say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 149.4,
          "end": 153.15,
          "en": "And I expect to get the selected place",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 153.15,
          "end": 157.353,
          "en": "which will be of type place as a parameter here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 158.49,
          "end": 163.11,
          "en": "Well, and now with that we can and should of course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 163.11,
          "end": 165.063,
          "en": "send such a put request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 166.14,
          "end": 170.1,
          "en": "So again, we can use the httpClient and then the put method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 170.1,
          "end": 171.753,
          "en": "to send such a request,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 172.59,
          "end": 177.59,
          "en": "and send that to http://localhost:3000/user-places.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 181.23,
          "end": 184.593,
          "en": "That is the route that's exposed by that backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 186.69,
          "end": 190.5,
          "en": "Now put then also needs a second argument, which is the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 190.5,
          "end": 192.873,
          "en": "that should be attached to that request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 193.92,
          "end": 195.99,
          "en": "Now you could attach an empty object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 195.99,
          "end": 198.57,
          "en": "if you have no real data you want to send.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 198.57,
          "end": 203.57,
          "en": "But in this case here, this route expects a request body",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 204.63,
          "end": 206.403,
          "en": "that contains a place ID.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 210,
          "end": 214.29,
          "en": "So in the Angular code, you should add a place ID key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 214.29,
          "end": 217.98,
          "en": "to that object and the data you send here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 217.98,
          "end": 220.07999999999998,
          "en": "by the way, doesn't have to be an object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 220.07999999999998,
          "end": 221.34,
          "en": "it could also be an array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 221.34,
          "end": 224.55,
          "en": "But here, we need an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 224.55,
          "end": 227.643,
          "en": "and that object should have a place ID property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 228.57,
          "end": 232.47,
          "en": "And Angular will automatically convert this object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 232.47,
          "end": 236.88,
          "en": "to JSON data using the JSON data format",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 236.88,
          "end": 239.34,
          "en": "to attach it to the outgoing request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 239.34,
          "end": 240.903,
          "en": "and send it to the backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 241.77,
          "end": 244.11,
          "en": "Now of course we need to define the value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 244.11,
          "end": 246.03,
          "en": "for that place ID property here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 246.03,
          "end": 249.033,
          "en": "and that should be selectedPlace.id.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 250.23,
          "end": 253.53,
          "en": "So the ID of the selected place on which the user clicked,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 253.53,
          "end": 257.01,
          "en": "that's set as a value for this place ID property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 257.01,
          "end": 261.36,
          "en": "in this object that is attached as JSON data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 261.36,
          "end": 263.61,
          "en": "to this outgoing put request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 263.61,
          "end": 265.653,
          "en": "That's what's happening here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 268.26,
          "end": 270.39,
          "en": "Now, if you would save it like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 270.39,
          "end": 273.51,
          "en": "nothing would happen if you click on a place though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 273.51,
          "end": 277.52,
          "en": "If you do that and you take a look at your network tab here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 277.52,
          "end": 281.463,
          "en": "in the dev tools, you won't see any new request here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 282.54,
          "end": 286.29,
          "en": "And the reason for that is that just as with get requests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 286.29,
          "end": 289.623,
          "en": "you need to subscribe to a request to trigger it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 290.46,
          "end": 292.59000000000003,
          "en": "So even though it's a put request,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 292.59000000000003,
          "end": 297.12,
          "en": "and we might not necessarily be interested in the response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 297.12,
          "end": 299.43,
          "en": "though, we also might be interested,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 299.43,
          "end": 301.44,
          "en": "but let's say we're not, even then,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 301.44,
          "end": 305.31,
          "en": "you have to subscribe to trigger that request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 305.31,
          "end": 306.45,
          "en": "Now just as before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 306.45,
          "end": 309.42,
          "en": "you can of course add your observer object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 309.42,
          "end": 312.45,
          "en": "to be notified once the request is complete,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 312.45,
          "end": 314.04,
          "en": "if there is an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 314.04,
          "end": 317.88,
          "en": "or about the next value that's emitted,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 317.88,
          "end": 319.68,
          "en": "which would be the response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 319.68,
          "end": 321.9,
          "en": "Because even though if you are not interested",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 321.9,
          "end": 326.1,
          "en": "in the response, or maybe even if there wouldn't be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 326.1,
          "end": 330.33,
          "en": "a meaningful response or no meaningful data sent back,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 330.33,
          "end": 333.72,
          "en": "even in those cases you would still get one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 333.72,
          "end": 336.69,
          "en": "And you could still output that response data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 336.69,
          "end": 339.183,
          "en": "if there was any like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 340.71,
          "end": 342.693,
          "en": "So that is always an option.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 343.86,
          "end": 346.83,
          "en": "But with that, this request will now be sent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 346.83,
          "end": 349.26,
          "en": "whenever this method is triggered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 349.26,
          "end": 351.99,
          "en": "Therefore, if you save that and reload",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 351.99,
          "end": 354.12,
          "en": "and you wait for those places to arrive,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 354.12,
          "end": 356.22,
          "en": "if you clear the network tab",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 356.22,
          "end": 359.04,
          "en": "so that we see a new request instantly,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 359.04,
          "end": 360.72,
          "en": "if you click on a place,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 360.72,
          "end": 363.33,
          "en": "you see there is a new request sent here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 363.33,
          "end": 367.26,
          "en": "this request, you can see that the payload of it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 367.26,
          "end": 370.05,
          "en": "is this object with a place ID key,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 370.05,
          "end": 371.673,
          "en": "which contains the place ID,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 372.57,
          "end": 375.78,
          "en": "and you can see the response that's sent back,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 375.78,
          "end": 379.653,
          "en": "which would be an object with the updated user-places.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 381,
          "end": 382.95,
          "en": "In addition, if you go to the backend code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 382.95,
          "end": 386.13,
          "en": "you can see that in the user-places.json file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 386.13,
          "end": 387.93,
          "en": "it's no longer an empty array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 387.93,
          "end": 391.323,
          "en": "but instead this place object has been added there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 392.28,
          "end": 396.12,
          "en": "And that all proves that sending this request worked.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 396.12,
          "end": 400.53,
          "en": "And that's how easy it is to send data to the backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 400.53,
          "end": 403.35,
          "en": "And of course you could and typically should now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 403.35,
          "end": 406.68,
          "en": "still also handle loading states",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 406.68,
          "end": 408.87,
          "en": "in case handling that submitted data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 408.87,
          "end": 410.88,
          "en": "takes a bit longer on the backend,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 410.88,
          "end": 414.45,
          "en": "and also handle potential errors.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 414.45,
          "end": 417.51,
          "en": "And we will do this later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 417.51,
          "end": 419.01,
          "en": "Before we do that though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 419.01,
          "end": 421.56,
          "en": "I wanna make sure that we also see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 421.56,
          "end": 425.25,
          "en": "those user-places here in this favorite places box,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 425.25,
          "end": 427.473,
          "en": "and that'll be the next step.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
